  "plan": "# WebUI Key Authentication Implementation Plan\n\n## Overview\nImplement a modal overlay prompting for the dashboard key, stored in localStorage. Without a valid key, the backend must not send any actual data to the frontend.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Fix Critical Modal Rendering Bug\n\n**Issue**: The key modal (index.html lines 250-257) is INSIDE the `{{if .Authenticated}}` block (line 210). Unauthenticated users see a blank page.\n\n**Solution**:\n1. Restructure index.html to move key modal outside the `{{if .Authenticated}}` block\n2. Add a separate `{{if .ShowKeyModal}}` or unconditionally render the modal container\n3. Use JavaScript to show/hide the modal based on auth state\n\n**Implementation**:\n- Move modal HTML to appear BEFORE the `{{if .Authenticated}}` conditional in index.html\n- Keep modal in its own conditional that evaluates independently of authenticated state\n- Backend passes `DashboardKeyConfigured` boolean to template (not just `Authenticated`)\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Fix Data Leakage - Server-Side Auth Enforcement\n\n**Issue**: api.go:139-153 fetches ALL clients/features before checking auth. Data is sent to browser but hidden with CSS.\n\n**Solution**:\n1. Modify the root handler (api.go:125-159) to check authentication BEFORE fetching data\n2. If not authenticated, render minimal page with modal but NO client/feature data\n3. Return appropriate HTTP status (401) for API calls without valid key\n\n**Implementation**:\n```go\n// In registerRoutes, for "/" handler (api.go:125-159)\nkey := r.URL.Query().Get(\"key\")\nauthenticated := key != \"\" && (cfg.DashboardKey == \"\" || key == cfg.DashboardKey)\n\nif !authenticated {\n    // Only render modal, no data\n    data := map[string]interface{}{\n        \"Key\":           \"\",\n        \"Authenticated\": false,\n        \"ShowKeyModal\":  cfg.DashboardKey != \"\", // Always show modal when key is required\n        \"Clients\":       []Client{}, // Empty data\n        \"StageGroups\":   []StageGroup{},\n    }\n    // Render template (but modal will show due to ShowKeyModal)\n    return\n}\n// Only fetch data if authenticated\nclients := hub.ListClients()\n// ... rest of data fetching\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Add Client Page Authentication\n\n**Issue**: serveClientPage (api.go:530) does NOT validate dashboard key. Any user can access /clients/{id} without authentication.\n\n**Solution**:\n1. Add checkDashboardAuth call at the start of serveClientPage\n2. Pass authentication state to client.html template\n3. If unauthenticated, render minimal page with modal (similar to dashboard)\n\n**Implementation**:\n```go\nfunc serveClientPage(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request, hub *Hub, tmpl *template.Template, cfg *Config) {\n    key := r.URL.Query().Get(\"key\")\n    authenticated := key != \"\" && (cfg.DashboardKey == \"\" || key == cfg.DashboardKey)\n    \n    // Add authentication check\n    if cfg.DashboardKey != \"\" && !authenticated {\n        // Render minimal page with modal but no data\n        data := map[string]interface{}{\n            \"ClientID\":      \"\",\n            \"Features\":      []FeatureSummary{},\n            \"StageGroups\":   []StageGroup{},\n            \"Logs\":          []LogEntry{},\n            \"Key\":           \"\",\n            \"Authenticated\": false,\n            \"ShowKeyModal\":  true,\n        }\n        // ... render template\n        return\n    }\n    // ... rest of existing logic\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Add Logout/Clear Key Functionality\n\n**Issue**: User requested logout/clear key option in UI.\n\n**Solution**:\n1. Add logout button to header area (visible when authenticated)\n2. Add clearKey() JavaScript function to remove 'mad_key' from localStorage\n3. Reload page after clearing to return to unauthenticated state\n\n**Implementation**:\n- Add to index.html header area:\n```html\n{{if .Authenticated}}\n<button onclick=\"logout()\" style=\"...\">Logout</button>\n{{end}}\n```\n\n- Add JavaScript function:\n```javascript\nfunction logout() {\n    if (confirm('Clear your saved key?')) {\n        localStorage.removeItem('mad_key');\n        // Clear URL params without reloading\n        window.history.replaceState({}, '', window.location.pathname);\n        location.reload();\n    }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: Add Invalid Key Error Feedback\n\n**Issue**: When user enters wrong key, no error message is shown. Page just reloads.\n\n**Solution**:\n1. Add error message display in the key modal\n2. On saveKey(), validate key against server before saving\n3. Show error if validation fails\n\n**Implementation**:\n- Add `/api/auth/validate` endpoint:\n```go\nmux.HandleFunc(\"/api/auth/validate\", func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n    key := r.URL.Query().Get(\"key\")\n    if cfg.DashboardKey == \"\" || key == cfg.DashboardKey {\n        writeJSON(w, http.StatusOK, map[string]bool{\"valid\": true})\n    } else {\n        writeJSON(w, http.StatusUnauthorized, map[string]bool{\"valid\": false})\n    }\n})\n```\n\n- Modify saveKey() in index.html:\n```javascript\nfunction saveKey() {\n    var input = document.getElementById('key-input');\n    var k = input.value.trim();\n    if (!k) return;\n    \n    // Validate key before saving\n    fetch('/api/auth/validate?key=' + encodeURIComponent(k))\n        .then(function(r) { return r.json(); })\n        .then(function(data) {\n            if (data.valid) {\n                localStorage.setItem('mad_key', k);\n                document.getElementById('key-modal').classList.remove('active');\n                location.reload();\n            } else {\n                document.getElementById('key-error').textContent = 'Invalid key';\n                document.getElementById('key-error').style.display = 'block';\n            }\n        })\n        .catch(function() {\n            // Network error - allow save anyway, server will reject later\n            localStorage.setItem('mad_key', k);\n            location.reload();\n        });\n}\n```\n\n- Add error display to modal HTML:\n```html\n<div id=\"key-error\" style=\"color:#f85149;font-size:0.85rem;margin-bottom:0.5rem;display:none\"></div>\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 6: Handle LocalStorage Unavailable\n\n**Issue**: Private browsing mode or disabled localStorage can cause errors.\n\n**Solution**:\n1. Wrap localStorage calls in try/catch\n2. Fall back to session-only key storage or show warning\n\n**Implementation**:\n```javascript\nfunction getKey() {\n    try {\n        var urlKey = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('key');\n        if (urlKey) {\n            localStorage.setItem('mad_key', urlKey);\n            return urlKey;\n        }\n        return localStorage.getItem('mad_key') || '';\n    } catch (e) {\n        // localStorage unavailable\n        return new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('key') || '';\n    }\n}\n\nfunction saveKey() {\n    try {\n        localStorage.setItem('mad_key', k);\n    } catch (e) {\n        alert('LocalStorage unavailable. Key will not persist after closing browser.');\n    }\n    // ... rest\n}\n\nfunction logout() {\n    try {\n        localStorage.removeItem('mad_key');\n    } catch (e) { /* ignore */ }\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 7: WebSocket Dashboard Key Support\n\n**Issue**: WebSocket handler (api.go:279-294) only validates APIKey, not DashboardKey.\n\n**Solution**:\n- Currently, WebSocket is used for real-time client connections (not dashboard data). Dashboard key is for web UI access, not real-time connections. If dashboard key is required for WebSocket, add validation:\n\n```go\nmux.HandleFunc(\"/ws\", func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n    authorized := false\n    // Check APIKey (existing logic)\n    if cfg.APIKey == \"\" {\n        authorized = true\n    } else {\n        if r.URL.Query().Get(\"api_key\") == cfg.APIKey {\n            authorized = true\n        } else if checkAPIAuth(r, cfg.APIKey) {\n            authorized = true\n        }\n    }\n    // If dashboard key is required for WebSocket access, add check\n    if !authorized && cfg.DashboardKey != \"\" {\n        if checkDashboardAuth(r, cfg.DashboardKey) {\n            authorized = true\n        }\n    }\n    // ... rest of handler\n})\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 8: HTMX Endpoint Protection\n\n**Issue**: /api/clients (api.go:201) uses checkAPIAuth, not checkDashboardAuth. Data could leak via HTMX requests.\n\n**Solution**:\n- The HTMX endpoints should respect dashboard key when DashboardKey is configured\n- Modify apiClientsHandler to also check dashboard auth:\n\n```go\nfunc apiClientsHandler(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n    // Check both APIKey and DashboardKey\n    if !checkAPIAuth(r, cfg.APIKey) && !checkDashboardAuth(r, cfg.DashboardKey) {\n        writeJSON(w, http.StatusUnauthorized, map[string]string{\"error\": \"unauthorized\"})\n        return\n    }\n    // ... rest of handler\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Order\n\n1. Phase 1 - Fix modal rendering (critical bug)\n2. Phase 2 - Fix data leakage (security critical)\n3. Phase 3 - Client page auth (security gap)\n4. Phase 4 - Logout button (user request)\n5. Phase 5 - Error feedback (UX improvement)\n6. Phase 6 - LocalStorage fallback (edge case)\n7. Phase 7 - WebSocket (if needed)\n8. Phase 8 - HTMX endpoints (security)\n\n---\n\n## Files to Modify\n\n1. `server/api.go` - Auth checks, data leakage fix, client page auth\n2. `server/templates/index.html` - Modal placement, logout button, error display, JS functions\n3. `server/templates/client.html` - Add key modal and auth check (or reuse from shared template)\n\n---\n\n## Test Scenarios\n\n1. DashboardKey configured, no key in URL/localStorage → Modal appears, no data in page source\n2. DashboardKey configured, valid key entered → Modal hidden, dashboard shows data\n3. DashboardKey configured, invalid key entered → Error message shown\n4. DashboardKey configured, logout clicked → Key cleared, modal appears\n5. DashboardKey NOT configured → Modal never appears, no auth required\n6. Client page without key → Modal appears, no data shown\n7. localStorage unavailable → Works without persistence\n8. Network error during validation → Allows save, lets server validate on next request"
}
